{
  "suite": "node",
  "version": "1.7.0",
  "description": "v1.7.0 (beta): node request signatures and what an edge agent verifies. A node signs the canonical JSON of its request body without 'signature' (sorted keys, no whitespace, ASCII escapes, Python float form) with its node key. At /join an edge node's executor key first signs the body without 'signature' and 'executor_signature'; the node key then signs the body including 'executor_signature'. The /node/* routes also sign 'purpose' and 'audience' (the NA public key). Keys: node 'a', executor 'b', NA 'c' (the fixed seeds). Kinds: 'node_request' (input.body is signed by input.node_key; expected payload and signature), 'join_request' (also expected executor_payload, executor_signature_b64 and executor_key_id), 'node_request_tampered' (input.signature_b64 over another body; expected verifies), 'join_certificate' and 'crl' (a record signed by the NA; expected the canonical payload, without 'signatures', and whether it verifies with input.na_public_keys).",
  "vectors": [
    {
